# VIGIL automated backup — environment file (copy to ~/.config/vigil/backup.env, chmod 600)
# =====================================================================
# Read by vigil-backup.service. Two settings:
#
#   VIGIL_BACKUP_PASSPHRASE — the ONLY key to the encrypted backups. It is read
#       from the ENVIRONMENT by both legs (offense + the sovereign sigil
#       subprocess) and is NEVER passed on the command line. It is NEVER stored
#       inside the backup — lose it and the backups are UNRECOVERABLE by design
#       (that is the off-box confidentiality guarantee).
#
#   VIGIL_BASE_DIR — the offense engine home to back up (default .vigil-live,
#       relative to WorkingDirectory=%h/vigil). Give an ABSOLUTE path if yours
#       lives elsewhere.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# HONEST WARNING — an at-rest passphrase is weaker than an interactive one.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# A passphrase sitting in a 0600 env file is only as strong as that file's
# perms + disk-at-rest protection: any process running as your user, a stolen
# unencrypted disk, or a backup of THIS file leaks it, and then the encrypted
# backups are decryptable. This is a deliberate trade-off for UNATTENDED daily
# backups. To reduce the exposure:
#
#   * keep this file 0600 and owned by the backup user only (chmod 600);
#   * keep an INDEPENDENT offsite copy of the passphrase (a password manager /
#     sealed envelope) — if you lose it, the backups are worthless;
#   * PREFER systemd credentials over a plaintext env var where you can:
#         systemd-creds encrypt --name=vigil-backup-pass passphrase.txt backup.cred
#     then load it in the unit with `LoadCredentialEncrypted=` and read it from
#     $CREDENTIALS_DIRECTORY instead of a plaintext env var;
#   * for the strongest posture, drop the timer and run `vigil backup`
#     INTERACTIVELY (it prompts for the passphrase, never storing it).

VIGIL_BACKUP_PASSPHRASE=change-me-to-a-long-random-passphrase
VIGIL_BASE_DIR=.vigil-live
